{
  "answerable": true,
  "answer": "Not for sleeping, I'm afraid. With the rear seats in, the BikerBed works as a sofa, and there's enough headroom to sit up comfortably. To fully extend it into a bed and sleep on it, you'll need to take the rear seats out. In a standard-length VW Transporter (T5/T6), the BikerBed sits behind the rear seats, and when fully extended it takes up the whole rear of the van. Swapping back is fairly quick: once it's set up the first time, the BikerBed can be removed or refitted in under 30 minutes. An extra pair of hands helps, but you can do it on your own.",
